From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: allow a DT-gated host-only role workaround

Some board firmware sends a device-role notification while the port is being
used as a host. The resulting role transition can tear down xHCI. Provide a
device-tree-gated workaround for bring-up kernels while the firmware behavior
is investigated.

---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/drd.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/drd.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/drd.c
index 000000000000..000000000000 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/drd.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/drd.c
@@ -450,6 +450,12 @@ static int dwc3_usb_role_switch_set(struct usb_role_switch *sw,
 	struct dwc3 *dwc = usb_role_switch_get_drvdata(sw);
 	u32 mode;
 
+	if (role == USB_ROLE_DEVICE &&
+		device_property_read_bool(dwc->dev, "qcom,force-host-role")) {
+		dev_warn_once(dwc->dev,
+			      "forcing USB host role for board bring-up\n");
+		role = USB_ROLE_HOST;
+	}
+
 	switch (role) {
 	case USB_ROLE_HOST:
 		mode = DWC3_GCTL_PRTCAP_HOST;
-- 
2.50.1
